"Let $\\mathbb{L}^d$ denote the $d$-dimensional lattice. Define\n\n$$\nr_0(2)=2,\\qquad r_0(d)=3\\quad\\text{for all }d\\geq 3.\n$$\n\nLet $d\\in\\mathbb{N}$ with $d\\geq 2$, and let $r\\in\\mathbb{N}$ with $r\\geq r_0(d)$. **Component-size conjecture.** With high probability, the largest component of $G_n(\\mathbb{L}^d,r)$ has order\n\n$$\n\\Theta_{d,r}\\!\\left(n^{1/(d+1)}\\log n\\right).\n$$\n\nThis is proposed as a refinement of the preceding largest-component results, which give the corresponding phenomenon in a less precise or more general setting; the asserted asymptotic order remains conjectural."